title RecruitBook Batch 1 — Authentication, Role Identity & Protected Routing (Sequence)

' ============================================================
' PARTICIPANTS — exactly the six required, no more
' ============================================================

actor       "User / Browser"        as User
participant "RecruitBook App"        as App
participant "Supabase Auth"          as Auth   <<external>>
database    "RecruitBook Database"   as DB
participant "Email Service"          as Email  <<external>>
actor       "Platform Administrator" as Admin

autonumber

note over Auth, DB
  Supabase Auth handles credentials and sessions.
  RecruitBook Database stores role and account_status.
  Authentication is NOT authorization.
end note

' ============================================================
== Registration and Email Verification ==
' ============================================================

User -> App : Submit email, password, selected role
App -> App : Validate selected role against\npublic role allowlist

alt Role not allowed (Platform Administrator selected)
  App --> User : Reject registration\n(admins cannot self-register)
  note over App
    Public users cannot register as
    Platform Administrator. Admin
    accounts are seeded / manually
    provisioned.
  end note
else Allowed public role (Student / Counselor / Admissions Officer)
  App -> Auth : Sign-up request (email, password)
  Auth -> Auth : Create auth user
  Auth -> Email : Trigger verification email
  Email --> User : Deliver verification link
  App -> DB : Create application user profile
  App -> DB : Store role + account_status = email_unverified
  Auth --> App : Sign-up accepted

  User -> Auth : Click verification link
  Auth -> Auth : Validate verification token

  alt Email verification succeeds
    Auth --> App : Email verified
    App -> DB : Confirm account_status by role:\nStudent → active\nCounselor → pending_approval\nAdmissions Officer → pending_approval
    App --> User : Verified — proceed to login
  else Token invalid / expired / already used
    Auth --> App : Verification failed
    App --> User : Show verification error\n(request a new link)
  end
end

' ============================================================
== Login and Role-Based Redirect ==
' ============================================================

User -> App : Submit login credentials
App -> Auth : Authenticate credentials

alt Authentication failed
  Auth --> App : Auth failure
  App --> User : Show login error
else Authentication succeeds
  Auth --> App : Valid session (token)
  App -> DB : Query application user profile
  alt Missing application profile
    DB --> App : No profile found
    App --> User : Account recovery / error state
  else Profile exists
    DB --> App : Return role + account_status
    alt Suspended or invalid role/status combination
      App --> User : Redirect to /unauthorized
    else Valid role/status
      App --> User : Redirect per routing table
      note over App, DB
        Routing table (role + account_status → route):
        Student + active                      → /student/dashboard
        Counselor + pending_approval          → /counselor/pending
        Counselor + verified                  → /counselor/dashboard
        Admissions Officer + pending_approval → /admissions/pending
        Admissions Officer + verified         → /admissions/dashboard
        Platform Administrator + active/verified → /admin/dashboard
        suspended / invalid combination       → /unauthorized
      end note
    end
  end
end

' ============================================================
== Protected Dashboard Request ==
' ============================================================

User -> App : Request protected dashboard route
App -> Auth : Check Supabase session

alt No valid session
  Auth --> App : Session missing / expired
  App --> User : Redirect to /login
else Valid session
  Auth --> App : Session valid
  App -> DB : Read role + account_status
  DB --> App : Return role + account_status
  App -> App : Compare requested route\nvs required role/status
  alt Unauthorized role/status
    App --> User : Redirect to /unauthorized
  else Authorized role/status
    App --> User : Render requested dashboard
  end
end

note over App, DB
  UI hiding is not authorization.
  Protected routes must enforce
  server-side / middleware / layout
  role and account_status checks.
end note

' ============================================================
== Admin Approval and Suspension ==
' ============================================================

Admin -> App : Open admin dashboard
App -> Auth : Verify admin session
Auth --> App : Session valid
App -> DB : Read admin role + account_status
DB --> App : Return role + account_status

alt Admin not authorized
  App --> Admin : Redirect to /unauthorized
else Admin authorized
  App --> Admin : Render /admin/dashboard

  opt Approval action
    Admin -> App : Approve pending counselor /\nadmissions officer account
    App -> DB : Update account_status\npending_approval → verified
    App -> DB : Record audit log entry (approval)
    App --> Admin : Approval confirmed
  end

  opt Suspension action
    Admin -> App : Suspend user account
    App -> DB : Update account_status → suspended
    App -> DB : Record audit log entry (suspension)
    App --> Admin : Suspension confirmed
    note over App, DB
      Suspended user is denied all future
      protected dashboard access (see
      Protected Dashboard Request).
    end note
  end
end

' ============================================================
== Password Reset and Logout ==
' ============================================================

User -> App : Request password reset
App -> Auth : Start password reset
Auth -> Email : Send password reset email
Email --> User : Deliver reset link
User -> Auth : Click reset link
Auth -> Auth : Validate reset token

alt Token invalid / expired / used
  Auth --> App : Reset failed
  App --> User : Show reset error
else Token valid
  User -> Auth : Submit new password
  Auth -> Auth : Update password
  Auth --> App : Password updated
  App --> User : Return to login
  note over Auth, DB
    Password reset changes credentials,
    not RecruitBook role / account_status.
  end note
end

User -> App : Log out
App -> Auth : Sign out
Auth -> Auth : Invalidate session
Auth --> App : Session invalidated
App --> User : Redirect to login / public landing page

